2a8","file":"preprints/Single-fold-Diophantine-representations-September-24-2026/build/main.tex","line":56,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"bcdcbbb2b0781dc67841784a70849168a5685b28746f49bd88d3de67be933076","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Single-fold-Diophantine-representations-September-24-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:29afbba11e4a745c5d4e85bf8e819c09196733cd880dacd29965d15f4cd282a8","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Single-fold-Diophantine-representations-September-24-2026/build/main.tex#L56"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every integer $n\\ge1$ and every recursively enumerable set\n$S\\subseteq\\NN^n$, there are an integer $m\\ge1$ and a polynomial\n$P\\in\\ZZ[A_1,\\ldots,A_n,W_1,\\ldots,W_m]$ such that, for every $a\\in\\NN^n$,\n\\[\n \\#\\{w\\in\\NN^m:P(a,w)=0\\}=\n \\begin{cases}1,&a\\in S,\\\\0,&a\\notin S.\\end{cases}\n\\]"}
